      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tstd::vector<int> mat(n*n);\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &mat[i*n+j]);\n\n\tconst int W = n+1;\n\tstd::vector<long long> P(W*W, 0LL);\n\n\t// Build 2D prefix sums (P is (n+1)x(n+1), row-major)\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++){\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++){\n\t\t\tP[(i+1)*W + (j+1)] = P[i*W + (j+1)] + P[(i+1)*W + j] - P[i*W + j] + mat[i*n+j];\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tlong long mx = LLONG_MIN;\n\tconst int limit_i = n-s;\n\tconst int limit_j = n-s;\n\n\t// Parallelize over starting rows; each row computes its own diff vector and SIMD max reduction.\n\t#pragma omp parallel for reduction(max:mx) schedule(static)\n\tfor(int i=0;i<=limit_i;i++){\n\t\tconst long long* __restrict__ top = &P[i*W];\n\t\tconst long long* __restrict__ bot = &P[(i+s)*W];\n\n\t\t// diff[k] = vertical sum of rows i..i+S-1 for column k (prefix form)\n\t\tlong long diff[8001]; // n < 8000, so this is safe and avoids heap allocation per iteration\n\t\t#pragma omp simd\n\t\tfor(int k=0;k<=n;k++){\n\t\t\tdiff[k] = bot[k] - top[k];\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tlong long localMax = LLONG_MIN;\n\t\t// Each submatrix sum is independent: diff[j+S] - diff[j]\n\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(max:localMax)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<=limit_j;j++){\n\t\t\tlong long sum = diff[j+s] - diff[j];\n\t\t\tif(sum > localMax) localMax = sum;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tmx = std::max(mx, localMax);\n\t}\n\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\", mx);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Using a flat row-major matrix and a 2D prefix-sum table, then parallelizing over starting rows with OpenMP while vectorizing the independent per-row max reduction via an explicit SIMD loop over column offsets (with a precomputed vertical-difference array to reduce memory traffic), will outperform the previous prefix-sum implementation by improving cache locality and enabling cleaner auto-vectorization of the inner query loop.",
  "notes": "The transformation replaces the original O(S*N^2) sliding-window code with an O(N^2) integral-image approach. The matrix is stored in a flat std::vector<int> for better spatial locality. Prefix sums use long long to avoid overflow (the problem only guarantees the final SxS sum fits 32-bit, not intermediate rectangles). The outer loop over starting rows is parallelized with OpenMP reduction(max:mx); each row computes a private diff array of vertical prefix differences and then uses #pragma omp simd reduction(max) on the independent column queries. This preserves exact output while exposing both thread-level parallelism and SIMD vectorization without introducing loop-carried dependencies in the hot query loop.",
